# Filtering and interpolation of time series movement signal generated by joint keypoints found through MeTRABS
# Experiment with different filters to remove noise and jittering -> moving average, moving MAD + median, lowpass butterworth, etc.
# Experiment with different interpolation methods to fill missing keypoints -> spline, cubic, linear

# The idea is to have multiple different pipelines for groups of joints to account for variations in movements across different parts of the body
# group 1 - head, spine 1, neck (upper body)
# group 2 - hips, spines 2 + 3 (lower body)
# group 3 - shoulders, elbow (upper arms)
# group 4 - wrists, hands (lower arms)

matplotlib.use('TkAgg')

